    { "day": -18, "at": "21:05", "do": "entry", "key": "e02",
      "text": "The green paths down the hill-sides are channels for streams. The young wheat is streaked by silver lines of water running between the ridges, the sheep are gathered together on the slopes. After the wet dark days, the country seems more populous. It peoples itself in the sunbeams.",
      "_source": { "book": "Journals of Dorothy Wordsworth, Vol. 1", "date": "20 January 1798" } },

    { "day": -17, "at": "08:15", "do": "entry", "key": "e03",
      "text": "At my office as I was receiving money of the probate of wills, in came Mrs. Turner, Theoph., Madame Morrice, and Joyce, and after I had done I took them home to my house and Mr. Hawly came after, and I got a dish of steaks and a rabbit for them, while they were playing a game or two at cards.",
      "_source": { "book": "The Diary of Samuel Pepys", "date": "7 January 1659-60" } },

    { "day": -16, "at": "10:00", "do": "task_add", "key": "insurance", "title": "Check the car insurance renewal", "list": "errands", "due": null },

    { "day": -15, "at": "10:30", "do": "entry", "key": "e04",
      "text": "Walked on the hill-tops--a warm day. Sate under the firs in the park. The tops of the beeches of a brown-red, or crimson.",
      "_source": { "book": "Journals of Dorothy Wordsworth, Vol. 1", "date": "21 January 1798" } },

    { "day": -14, "at": "18:00", "do": "task_add", "key": "tap", "title": "Fix the kitchen tap washer", "list": "home", "due": -7 },
    { "day": -14, "at": "20:40", "do": "entry", "key": "e05",
      "text": "For these two or three days I have been much troubled with thoughts how to get money to pay them that I have borrowed money of, by reason of my money being in my uncle’s hands.",
      "_source": { "book": "The Diary of Samuel Pepys", "date": "9 January 1659-60" } },

    { "day": -13, "at": "09:00", "do": "task_add", "key": "bins", "title": "Take the bins out", "list": "home", "due": -5 },
    { "day": -13, "at": "09:01", "do": "task_when", "key": "bins", "due": -5,
      "repeat": { "freq": "week", "every": 1, "days": null, "mode": "fixed" } },
    { "day": -13, "at": "11:00", "do": "task_add", "key": "passport", "title": "Renew passport", "list": "errands", "due": 4 },
    { "day": -13, "at": "12:30", "do": "task_complete", "key": "boiler_email" },
    { "day": -13, "at": "20:30", "do": "task_add", "key": "spare_room", "title": "Sort the spare room", "list": "home", "due": null },

    { "day": -12, "at": "07:55", "do": "entry", "key": "e06",
      "text": "Walked through the wood to Holford. The ivy twisting round the oaks like bristled serpents. The day cold--a warm shelter in the hollies, capriciously bearing berries.",
      "_source": { "book": "Journals of Dorothy Wordsworth, Vol. 1", "date": "22 January 1798" } },
    { "day": -12, "at": "10:00", "do": "task_add", "key": "library", "title": "Return the library books", "list": "errands", "due": -8 },

    { "day": -11, "at": "11:30", "do": "task_wont_do", "key": "insurance" },
    { "day": -11, "at": "21:10", "do": "entry", "key": "e07",
      "text": "In the morning I went up to Mr. Crew’s, and at his bedside he gave me direction to go to-morrow with Mr. Edward to Twickenham, and likewise did talk to me concerning things of state; and expressed his mind how just it was that the secluded members should come to sit again.",
      "_source": { "book": "The Diary of Samuel Pepys", "date": "16 January 1659-60" } },

    { "day": -10, "at": "09:15", "do": "task_add", "key": "invoice", "title": "Send the invoice to Harlow & Co", "list": "work", "due": -2 },
    { "day": -10, "at": "12:20", "do": "entry", "key": "e08",
      "text": "Early I went to Mr. Crew’s, and having given Mr. Edward money to give the servants, I took him into the coach that waited for us and carried him to my house, where the coach waited for me while I and the child went to Westminster Hall, and bought him some pictures.",
      "_source": { "book": "The Diary of Samuel Pepys", "date": "17 January 1659-60" } },
    { "day": -10, "at": "18:40", "do": "comment", "key": "passport", "body": "Photos first, then the form." },

    { "day": -9, "at": "12:00", "do": "task_add", "key": "lisbon", "title": "Plan the Lisbon trip", "list": null, "due": null },
    { "day": -9, "at": "14:00", "do": "task_add", "key": "q4_report", "title": "Draft the Q4 report", "list": "work", "due": 3 },

    { "day": -8, "at": "08:40", "do": "task_add", "key": "running_shoes", "title": "Order new running shoes", "list": "errands", "due": -7 },
    { "day": -8, "at": "09:00", "do": "entry", "key": "e09",
      "text": "To my office and from thence to Will’s, and there Mr. Sheply brought me letters from the carrier and so I went home.",
      "_source": { "book": "The Diary of Samuel Pepys", "date": "18 January 1659-60" } },
    { "day": -8, "at": "10:00", "do": "task_priority", "key": "q4_report", "priority": 1 },

    { "day": -7, "at": "19:05", "do": "task_complete", "key": "running_shoes" },
    { "day": -7, "at": "19:15", "do": "comment", "key": "tap", "body": "Bought the washer, it is on the shelf." },
    { "day": -7, "at": "19:45", "do": "entry", "key": "e10",
      "text": "Bright sunshine, went out at 3 o'clock. The sea perfectly calm blue, streaked with deeper colour by the clouds, and tongues or points of sand; on our return of a gloomy red. The sun gone down. The crescent moon, Jupiter, and Venus.",
      "_source": { "book": "Journals of Dorothy Wordsworth, Vol. 1", "date": "23 January 1798" } },
    { "day": -7, "at": "20:00", "do": "comment", "key": "spare_room", "body": "Bags to the charity shop by Friday." },

    { "day": -6, "at": "08:05", "do": "entry", "key": "e11",
      "text": "This morning I was sent for to Mr. Downing, and at his bed side he told me, that he had a kindness for me, and that he thought that he had done me one; and that was, that he had got me to be one of the Clerks of the Council; at which I was a little stumbled, and could not tell what to do, whether to thank him or no; but by and by I did; but not very heartily, for I feared that his doing of it was but only to ease himself of the salary which he gives me.",
      "_source": { "book": "The Diary of Samuel Pepys", "date": "19 January 1659-60" } },
    { "day": -6, "at": "19:00", "do": "task_add", "key": "violin", "title": "Learn the violin", "list": "home", "due": null },
    { "day": -6, "at": "21:00", "do": "task_add", "key": "card_birthday", "title": "Send Mum a birthday card", "list": "home", "due": 2 },

    { "day": -5, "at": "08:30", "do": "task_add", "key": "dentist", "title": "Book the dentist", "list": "errands", "due": 2 },
    { "day": -5, "at": "19:40", "do": "task_complete", "key": "bins" },
    { "day": -5, "at": "22:10", "do": "entry", "key": "e12",
      "text": "Up early in finishing my accounts and writing to my Lord and from thence to my Lord’s and took leave of Mr. Sheply and possession of all the keys and the house.",
      "_source": { "book": "The Diary of Samuel Pepys", "date": "21 January 1659-60" } },

    { "day": -3, "at": "07:50", "do": "task_add", "key": "plants", "title": "Water the plants", "list": "home", "due": -3 },
    { "day": -3, "at": "07:51", "do": "task_when", "key": "plants", "due": -3,
      "repeat": { "freq": "day", "every": 1, "days": null, "mode": "fixed" } },
    { "day": -3, "at": "07:55", "do": "task_complete", "key": "plants" },
