    { "day": -3, "at": "10:00", "do": "task_priority", "key": "invoice", "priority": 2 },
    { "day": -3, "at": "10:20", "do": "comment", "key": "invoice", "body": "Emailed the PDF; they say they will pay Monday." },
    { "day": -3, "at": "11:00", "do": "task_complete", "key": "library" },
    { "day": -3, "at": "17:30", "do": "task_add", "key": "dry_cleaning", "title": "Pick up the dry cleaning", "list": "home", "due": -1 },
    { "day": -3, "at": "18:20", "do": "entry", "key": "e13",
      "text": "I went in the morning to Mr. Messum’s, where I met with W. Thurburn and sat with him in his pew. A very eloquent sermon about the duty of all to give good example in our lives and conversation, which I fear he himself was most guilty of not doing.",
      "_source": { "book": "The Diary of Samuel Pepys", "date": "22 January 1659-60" } },

    { "day": -2, "at": "07:30", "do": "entry", "key": "e15", "page": -2,
      "text": "Walked between half-past three and half-past five. The evening cold and clear. The sea of a sober grey, streaked by the deeper grey clouds. The half dead sound of the near sheep-bell, in the hollow of the sloping coombe, exquisitely soothing.",
      "_source": { "book": "Journals of Dorothy Wordsworth, Vol. 1", "date": "24 January 1798" } },
    { "day": -2, "at": "08:00", "do": "task_skip", "key": "plants" },
    { "day": -2, "at": "09:40", "do": "task_add", "key": "draft_priya", "title": "Email Priya the draft", "list": null, "due": null },
    { "day": -2, "at": "12:00", "do": "task_add", "key": "vet", "title": "Call the vet about the booster", "list": "home", "due": 0 },
    { "day": -2, "at": "16:10", "do": "comment", "key": "q4_report", "body": "Outline done. Numbers from finance on Monday." },
    { "day": -2, "at": "20:05", "do": "entry", "key": "e14", "page": -2,
      "text": "In the morning called out to carry L20 to Mr. Downing, which I did and came back, and finding Mr. Pierce, the surgeon, I took him to the Axe and gave him his morning draft.",
      "_source": { "book": "The Diary of Samuel Pepys", "date": "23 January 1659-60" } },

    { "day": -1, "at": "00:40", "do": "entry", "key": "e16", "page": -2,
      "text": "Having been exceedingly disturbed in the night with the barking of a dog of one of our neighbours that I could not sleep for an hour or two, I slept late, and then in the morning took physic, and so staid within all day.",
      "_source": { "book": "The Diary of Samuel Pepys", "date": "15 January 1659-60" } },
    { "day": -1, "at": "07:55", "do": "task_complete", "key": "plants" },
    { "day": -1, "at": "08:30", "do": "entry_edit", "key": "e14",
      "text": "In the morning called out to carry L20 to Mr. Downing, which I did and came back, and finding Mr. Pierce, the surgeon, I took him to the Axe and gave him his morning draft. Thence to my office and there did nothing but make up my balance." },
    { "day": -1, "at": "09:02", "do": "task_add", "key": "call_bank", "title": "Call the bank about the card", "list": null, "due": null },
    { "day": -1, "at": "09:14", "do": "entry", "key": "e17",
      "text": "In the morning to my office, where, after I had drank my morning draft at Will’s with Ethell and Mr. Stevens, I went and told part of the excise money till twelve o’clock, and then called on my wife and took her to Mr. Pierces, she in the way being exceedingly troubled with a pair of new pattens, and I vexed to go so slow, it being late.",
      "_source": { "book": "The Diary of Samuel Pepys", "date": "24 January 1659-60" } },
    { "day": -1, "at": "09:30", "do": "task_when", "key": "council_tax", "due": 3 },
    { "day": -1, "at": "09:35", "do": "comment", "key": "council_tax", "body": "Moved to Wednesday, after payday." },
    { "day": -1, "at": "10:44", "do": "comment", "key": "call_bank", "body": "Card is blocked. New one posted, due Tuesday." },
    { "day": -1, "at": "10:45", "do": "task_complete", "key": "call_bank" },
